{
  "slug": "probabl-skills",
  "name": "Probabl Skills",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Skills to support Machine Learning experimentation using the Python ecosystem.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `audit-ml-pipeline` (Owns the `audit/` folder: one `# %%` (jupytext percent) Python file per experiment, aligned 1:1 with `experiments/NN_<short_name>.py` and…), `build-ml-pipeline` (Declare the pipeline from data source to predictor as a **skrub DataOps graph** (not as a bare `sklearn.Pipeline`)), `data-science-python-stack` (Opinionated Python stack for data-science / ML work — one library per job, organized into tiers (mandatory /…), `evaluate-ml-pipeline` (Methodology for evaluating a single sklearn-compatible learner (in particular, the `SkrubLearner` produced by `build-ml-pipeline`)), `explore-ml-data` (Owns data understanding BEFORE any model is designed), `iterate-from-skore` (Source the next ML experiment proposal by **reading the audit digest** at `scratch/audit/<stem>/audit.md` (produced by `audit-ml-pipeline` at §…), `iterate-from-user` (Source the next ML experiment proposal from the user via one of three entry points selected by `AskUserQuestion`:…), `iterate-ml-experiment` (Owns the iteration loop on top of an ML workspace: the `journal/JOURNAL.md` index and the per-experiment `journal/NN_short_name.md` design…), and 6 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install probabl-skills@claude-community` from `probabl-ai/skills`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
